{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Policy cross-links

  Rendered by layout/theme.liquid directly after content_for_layout, on
  request.page_type == 'policy' only. It cannot be a section: Shopify has no
  `policy` template type, so these five pages have no section list to add one to.

  shop.policies yields only the policies that actually exist, so a store that
  never writes a subscription policy simply gets four links instead of five —
  no blank rows, nothing to maintain.

  `contains` rather than `==` on the current path so a locale-prefixed URL
  (/en-in/policies/refund-policy) still matches its own /policies/refund-policy
  and drops out of the list.

  Styles live in assets/shudhi-policy.css, which theme.liquid has already
  loaded on this page.
{%- endcomment -%}

<nav class="sh sh-policy-links" aria-label="Store policies">
  <span class="sh-policy-links__label sh-eyebrow">More policies</span>

  {%- comment -%} role="list" is deliberate: the .sh reset strips list markers,
      and Safari/VoiceOver then drop list semantics entirely. Same reason
      sections/sh-feature-grid.liquid:72 carries it. {%- endcomment -%}
  <ul class="sh-policy-links__list" role="list">
    {%- for policy in shop.policies -%}
      {%- unless policy.body == blank or request.path contains policy.url -%}
        <li><a href="{{ policy.url }}">{{ policy.title }}</a></li>
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
</nav>
